     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "{'text': \"# Sunrise Institute of Technology (SIT) – College Overview\\n\\n## Basic Information\\n- College Name: Sunrise Institute of Technology (SIT)\\n- Established: 2005\\n- Affiliation: State Technical University\\n- Approved by: AICTE\\n- NAAC Grade: A\\n- Address: Plot 12, Knowledge Park, Sector 5, Greenfield City – 452001\\n- Campus Area: 25 acres\\n- Principal: Dr. Ramesh Kumar Verma\\n- Principal's Office: Admin Block, Ground Floor, Room A-001\\n- Official Website: www.sit-college.example.edu\\n- Main Office Phone: 0731-2400100\\n- Email: info@sit-college.example.edu\\n\\n## Courses Offered\\n### Undergraduate (B.Tech – 4 Years)\\n- Computer Science and Engineering (CSE) – 180 seats\\n- Information Technology (IT) – 120 seats\\n- Electronics and Communication Engineering (ECE) – 120 seats\\n- Mechanical Engineering (ME) – 60 seats\\n- Civil Engineering (CE) – 60 seats\\n- Artificial Intelligence and Data Science (AI&DS) – 60 seats\\n\\n### Postgraduate\\n- M.Tech in Computer Science (2 Years) – 18 seats\\n- MBA (2 Years) – 60 seats\\n- MCA (2 Years) – 60 seats\\n\\n## Campus Buildings\\n- Admin Block: Principal office, accounts section, admission cell, exam cell\\n- Block A: CSE and IT departments\\n- Block B: ECE and AI&DS departments\\n- Block C: Mechanical and Civil departments, workshops\\n- Block D: MBA and MCA departments\\n- Central Library: Separate building beside Block A\\n- Canteen: Behind Block B\\n- Auditorium: Near main gate (capacity 800)\\n- Sports Complex: East side of campus\\n- Boys Hostel: North campus\\n- Girls Hostel: South campus (near Block D)\\n\", 'source': '01_college_overview.md'}\n",
      "{'text': '# SIT Fee Structure – Academic Year 2026-27\\n\\n## B.Tech Fee Structure (Per Year)\\n| Fee Component        | Amount (INR) |\\n|----------------------|--------------|\\n| Tuition Fee          | 95,000       |\\n| Development Fee      | 10,000       |\\n| Exam Fee             | 4,000        |\\n| Library Fee          | 2,000        |\\n| Lab Fee              | 5,000        |\\n| Student Activity Fee | 2,000        |\\n| **Total per Year**   | **1,18,000** |\\n\\n- One-time Admission Fee (first year only): 10,000\\n- Refundable Caution Deposit (first year only): 5,000\\n- Total first-year B.Tech fee: 1,33,000\\n\\n## M.Tech Fee Structure (Per Year)\\n- Tuition Fee: 80,000\\n- Other Charges: 12,000\\n- Total per Year: 92,000\\n\\n## MBA Fee Structure (Per Year)\\n- Tuition Fee: 1,10,000\\n- Other Charges: 15,000\\n- Total per Year: 1,25,000\\n\\n## MCA Fee Structure (Per Year)\\n- Tuition Fee: 75,000\\n- Other Charges: 10,000\\n- Total per Year: 85,000\\n\\n## Hostel Fee (Per Year, includes mess)\\n- Triple sharing room (non-AC): 85,000\\n- Double sharing room (non-AC): 1,00,000\\n- Double sharing room (AC): 1,30,000\\n- Hostel security deposit (refundable, one time): 10,000\\n\\n## Transport (Bus) Fee (Per Year)\\n- Up to 10 km: 18,000\\n- 10 to 20 km: 25,000\\n- Above 20 km: 32,000\\n\\n## Fee Payment Rules\\n- Fees can be paid in two installments: 60% before 15 July and 40% before 15 December.\\n- Late fee: INR 100 per day after the due date, maximum INR 5,000.\\n- Payment modes: Online via student portal (UPI, net banking, card), Demand Draft in favour of \"Sunrise Institute of Technology\", or at the Accounts Section counter.\\n- Cash payment is NOT accepted above INR 20,000.\\n- Fee receipts are available on the student portal within 48 hours of payment.\\n\\n## Scholarships and Concessions\\n- Merit Scholarship: 50% tuition waiver for students with 95%+ in 12th or top 100 rank in entrance exam.\\n- Merit Scholarship: 25% tuition waiver for students with 90–94.99% in 12th.\\n- Continuation: Student must maintain CGPA 8.5 or above to keep the scholarship.\\n- Sibling Concession: 10% tuition waiver for the second child studying at SIT.\\n- Government scholarships (SC/ST/OBC/EWS) are handled by the Scholarship Cell, Admin Block, Room A-104.\\n\\n## Refund Policy\\n- Withdrawal before classes start: Full refund except INR 1,000 processing fee.\\n- Withdrawal within 15 days of classes starting: 80% refund of tuition fee.\\n- Withdrawal after 15 days: No refund of tuition fee; caution deposit is refunded.\\n\\n## Accounts Section Contact\\n- Location: Admin Block, Ground Floor, Room A-005\\n- Timing: Monday to Friday, 9:30 AM – 4:00 PM; Saturday 9:30 AM – 1:00 PM\\n- Accounts Officer: Mr. Suresh Patel\\n- Phone: 0731-2400105\\n- Email: accounts@sit-college.example.edu\\n', 'source': '02_fee_structure.md'}\n",
      "{'text': '# SIT College Timings and Schedule\\n\\n## Regular Class Timings\\n- Working Days: Monday to Saturday\\n- Saturday: Half day (classes till 1:00 PM). 2nd and 4th Saturday are holidays.\\n- Sunday: Holiday\\n\\n## Daily Lecture Schedule (Monday to Friday)\\n| Period         | Time               |\\n|----------------|--------------------|\\n| Period 1       | 9:00 AM – 9:55 AM  |\\n| Period 2       | 9:55 AM – 10:50 AM |\\n| Short Break    | 10:50 AM – 11:00 AM|\\n| Period 3       | 11:00 AM – 11:55 AM|\\n| Period 4       | 11:55 AM – 12:50 PM|\\n| Lunch Break    | 12:50 PM – 1:40 PM |\\n| Period 5       | 1:40 PM – 2:35 PM  |\\n| Period 6       | 2:35 PM – 3:30 PM  |\\n| Period 7 (Lab) | 3:30 PM – 4:25 PM  |\\n\\n## Saturday Schedule\\n- Period 1 to Period 4: 9:00 AM – 12:50 PM\\n- No lunch break; college closes at 1:00 PM.\\n\\n## Office Timings\\n- Admin Office: 9:30 AM – 5:00 PM (Mon–Fri), 9:30 AM – 1:00 PM (Sat)\\n- Accounts Section: 9:30 AM – 4:00 PM (Mon–Fri), 9:30 AM – 1:00 PM (Sat)\\n- Exam Cell: 10:00 AM – 4:00 PM (Mon–Fri)\\n- Admission Cell: 9:00 AM – 5:00 PM (Mon–Sat during admission season, June to August)\\n\\n## Facility Timings\\n- Central Library: 8:00 AM – 8:00 PM (Mon–Sat); 10:00 AM – 2:00 PM (Sunday, reading room only)\\n- Library during exams: Open till 10:00 PM\\n- Canteen: 8:00 AM – 6:00 PM (Mon–Sat)\\n- Computer Center (Block A, 2nd Floor): 9:00 AM – 7:00 PM\\n- Gym (Sports Complex): 6:00 AM – 8:00 AM and 5:00 PM – 8:00 PM\\n- Medical Room (Admin Block, Ground Floor): 9:00 AM – 5:00 PM, Nurse on duty; Doctor visits 11:00 AM – 1:00 PM on Mon, Wed, Fri\\n\\n## Academic Calendar 2026-27 (Important Dates)\\n- Odd Semester classes begin: 1 August 2026\\n- Mid-semester exams (Odd): 21 – 26 September 2026\\n- Diwali break: 6 – 12 November 2026\\n- End-semester exams (Odd): 1 – 15 December 2026\\n- Winter break: 16 December 2026 – 1 January 2027\\n- Even Semester classes begin: 4 January 2027\\n- Annual Tech Fest \"Techno-Rise\": 12 – 14 February 2027\\n- Mid-semester exams (Even): 22 – 27 February 2027\\n- End-semester exams (Even): 3 – 18 May 2027\\n- Summer vacation: 20 May – 31 July 2027\\n', 'source': '03_college_timings.md'}\n",
      "{'text': '# SIT Departments, HODs, Cabin Locations and Availability\\n\\nNote: \"Free hours\" are the times when the HOD is generally available to meet students without an appointment. For urgent matters outside these hours, contact the department office.\\n\\n## Computer Science and Engineering (CSE) Department\\n- HOD: Dr. Anjali Sharma\\n- Qualification: Ph.D. (Machine Learning), IIT Bombay\\n- HOD Cabin: Block A, 3rd Floor, Room A-301\\n- Department Office: Block A, 3rd Floor, Room A-302\\n- Email: hod.cse@sit-college.example.edu\\n- Phone (Extension): 0731-2400201\\n- HOD Free Hours for Students:\\n  - Monday: 2:35 PM – 4:00 PM\\n  - Wednesday: 11:00 AM – 12:50 PM\\n  - Friday: 1:40 PM – 3:30 PM\\n- Not available: Tuesday (University meetings), Saturday\\n\\n## Information Technology (IT) Department\\n- HOD: Dr. Vikram Singh Rathore\\n- Qualification: Ph.D. (Cyber Security), NIT Trichy\\n- HOD Cabin: Block A, 2nd Floor, Room A-210\\n- Department Office: Block A, 2nd Floor, Room A-211\\n- Email: hod.it@sit-college.example.edu\\n- Phone (Extension): 0731-2400202\\n- HOD Free Hours for Students:\\n  - Tuesday: 11:00 AM – 12:50 PM\\n  - Thursday: 2:35 PM – 4:25 PM\\n  - Saturday: 11:00 AM – 12:30 PM\\n\\n## Electronics and Communication Engineering (ECE) Department\\n- HOD: Dr. Meera Iyer\\n- Qualification: Ph.D. (VLSI Design), IISc Bangalore\\n- HOD Cabin: Block B, 1st Floor, Room B-105\\n- Department Office: Block B, 1st Floor, Room B-106\\n- Email: hod.ece@sit-college.example.edu\\n- Phone (Extension): 0731-2400203\\n- HOD Free Hours for Students:\\n  - Monday: 11:00 AM – 12:50 PM\\n  - Wednesday: 2:35 PM – 4:00 PM\\n  - Thursday: 9:00 AM – 10:50 AM\\n\\n## Artificial Intelligence and Data Science (AI&DS) Department\\n- HOD: Dr. Rohan Mehta\\n- Qualification: Ph.D. (Natural Language Processing), IIIT Hyderabad\\n- HOD Cabin: Block B, 3rd Floor, Room B-310\\n- Department Office: Block B, 3rd Floor, Room B-311\\n- Email: hod.aids@sit-college.example.edu\\n- Phone (Extension): 0731-2400204\\n- HOD Free Hours for Students:\\n  - Tuesday: 1:40 PM – 3:30 PM\\n  - Friday: 9:00 AM – 10:50 AM\\n\\n## Mechanical Engineering (ME) Department\\n- HOD: Dr. Prakash Joshi\\n- Qualification: Ph.D. (Thermal Engineering), IIT Kanpur\\n- HOD Cabin: Block C, Ground Floor, Room C-010\\n- Department Office: Block C, Ground Floor, Room C-011\\n- Email: hod.me@sit-college.example.edu\\n- Phone (Extension): 0731-2400205\\n- HOD Free Hours for Students:\\n  - Monday: 9:00 AM – 10:50 AM\\n  - Thursday: 11:00 AM – 12:50 PM\\n\\n## Civil Engineering (CE) Department\\n- HOD: Dr. Sunita Deshmukh\\n- Qualification: Ph.D. (Structural Engineering), VNIT Nagpur\\n- HOD Cabin: Block C, 1st Floor, Room C-120\\n- Department Office: Block C, 1st Floor, Room C-121\\n- Email: hod.ce@sit-college.example.edu\\n- Phone (Extension): 0731-2400206\\n- HOD Free Hours for Students:\\n  - Wednesday: 9:00 AM – 10:50 AM\\n  - Friday: 2:35 PM – 4:25 PM\\n\\n## MBA Department\\n- HOD: Dr. Kavita Nair\\n- Qualification: Ph.D. (Finance), Symbiosis Pune\\n- HOD Cabin: Block D, 1st Floor, Room D-101\\n- Email: hod.mba@sit-college.example.edu\\n- Phone (Extension): 0731-2400207\\n- HOD Free Hours for Students:\\n  - Monday to Friday: 4:00 PM – 5:00 PM\\n\\n## MCA Department\\n- HOD: Dr. Arjun Malhotra\\n- Qualification: Ph.D. (Software Engineering), DAVV Indore\\n- HOD Cabin: Block D, 2nd Floor, Room D-205\\n- Email: hod.mca@sit-college.example.edu\\n- Phone (Extension): 0731-2400208\\n- HOD Free Hours for Students:\\n  - Tuesday: 9:00 AM – 10:50 AM\\n  - Thursday: 1:40 PM – 3:30 PM\\n', 'source': '04_departments_and_hods.md'}\n",
      "{'text': '# SIT Admission Process 2026-27\\n\\n## B.Tech Admission Eligibility\\n- Passed 12th with Physics, Chemistry, and Mathematics.\\n- Minimum 60% aggregate in PCM (55% for SC/ST/OBC).\\n- Valid score in JEE Main or State Engineering Entrance Exam.\\n\\n## M.Tech Admission Eligibility\\n- B.Tech/B.E. in relevant branch with minimum 60% (or CGPA 6.5).\\n- Valid GATE score preferred; otherwise college entrance test.\\n\\n## MBA Admission Eligibility\\n- Any graduation with minimum 50% marks.\\n- Valid CAT / MAT / CMAT score, followed by Group Discussion and Personal Interview.\\n\\n## MCA Admission Eligibility\\n- BCA / B.Sc (CS/IT) / any graduation with Mathematics at 12th or graduation level, minimum 50%.\\n\\n## Admission Steps\\n1. Fill the online application form on www.sit-college.example.edu/admissions (Application fee: INR 1,000).\\n2. Upload documents: 10th & 12th marksheets, entrance exam scorecard, Aadhaar card, passport photo, category certificate (if any).\\n3. Attend counselling / document verification at the Admission Cell.\\n4. Pay first installment of fees to confirm the seat.\\n5. Collect ID card and student portal login from the Admin Office.\\n\\n## Important Admission Dates\\n- Application opens: 1 May 2026\\n- Last date to apply: 30 June 2026\\n- Counselling: 5 – 20 July 2026\\n- Classes begin: 1 August 2026\\n\\n## Admission Cell Contact\\n- Location: Admin Block, Ground Floor, Room A-002\\n- Admission In-charge: Prof. Neha Gupta\\n- Phone: 0731-2400110\\n- Email: admissions@sit-college.example.edu\\n', 'source': '05_admissions.md'}\n",
      "{'text': \"# SIT Hostel, Transport and Other Facilities\\n\\n## Boys Hostel\\n- Location: North campus\\n- Capacity: 600 students\\n- Warden: Mr. Rajesh Yadav (Phone: 0731-2400301)\\n- In-time: 9:30 PM\\n- Mess timings: Breakfast 7:30–9:00 AM, Lunch 12:45–2:00 PM, Snacks 5:00–6:00 PM, Dinner 8:00–9:30 PM\\n\\n## Girls Hostel\\n- Location: South campus, near Block D\\n- Capacity: 400 students\\n- Warden: Mrs. Pooja Saxena (Phone: 0731-2400302)\\n- In-time: 8:30 PM\\n- Mess timings: Same as Boys Hostel\\n\\n## Hostel Rules\\n- Night-out permission requires a parent's written consent and warden approval.\\n- Visitors allowed only on Sundays, 10:00 AM – 5:00 PM, in the visitor lounge.\\n- Wi-Fi available in all hostel rooms (40 Mbps per student).\\n- Ragging is strictly prohibited; anti-ragging helpline: 1800-180-5522.\\n\\n## Transport (College Bus)\\n- 15 buses covering 12 routes across the city.\\n- Buses leave campus at 4:35 PM (Mon–Fri) and 1:10 PM (Saturday).\\n- Bus pass is collected from the Transport Office, Admin Block, Room A-008.\\n- Transport In-charge: Mr. Dinesh Chouhan (Phone: 0731-2400120)\\n\\n## Central Library\\n- Location: Separate building beside Block A\\n- Books: 65,000+; e-journals: IEEE, Springer, Elsevier access\\n- Max books issued: 4 books for 14 days (UG), 6 books for 30 days (PG)\\n- Fine for late return: INR 5 per day per book\\n- Librarian: Mrs. Asha Kulkarni\\n\\n## Medical Facility\\n- Medical Room in Admin Block, Ground Floor.\\n- Ambulance available 24x7: 0731-2400999\\n\\n## Training and Placement Cell\\n- Location: Admin Block, 1st Floor, Room A-110\\n- Training & Placement Officer (TPO): Mr. Amit Bansal\\n- Phone: 0731-2400130\\n- Email: placement@sit-college.example.edu\\n- Timing: 10:00 AM – 5:00 PM (Mon–Fri)\\n- Placement 2025-26: 82% students placed; highest package 24 LPA; average package 6.2 LPA\\n- Top recruiters: TCS, Infosys, Wipro, Accenture, Capgemini, Amazon, Deloitte\\n\", 'source': '06_hostel_transport_facilities.md'}\n",
      "{'text': '# SIT Examination Rules and Academic Policies\\n\\n## Attendance Rules\\n- Minimum 75% attendance is required in each subject to appear in the end-semester exam.\\n- Students with 65–74% attendance may be allowed only with a valid medical certificate and HOD approval.\\n- Below 65% attendance: Detained; must repeat the subject.\\n\\n## Examination Pattern\\n- Mid-semester exam: 30 marks\\n- Internal assessment (assignments, quizzes, attendance): 20 marks\\n- End-semester exam: 50 marks (conducted by the university)\\n- Passing criteria: Minimum 40% in each subject (internal + external combined).\\n\\n## Re-evaluation and Supplementary Exams\\n- Re-evaluation application within 10 days of result declaration. Fee: INR 500 per subject.\\n- Supplementary (backlog) exams are held in July every year. Fee: INR 1,000 per subject.\\n\\n## Exam Cell\\n- Location: Admin Block, 1st Floor, Room A-115\\n- Controller of Examinations: Dr. Sanjay Tiwari\\n- Phone: 0731-2400140\\n- Email: examcell@sit-college.example.edu\\n- Timing: 10:00 AM – 4:00 PM (Mon–Fri)\\n\\n## Code of Conduct\\n- ID card must be worn at all times on campus.\\n- Mobile phones are not allowed in classrooms and exam halls.\\n- Dress code: Formal dress on Mondays and during placement drives.\\n- Ragging is a criminal offence and leads to immediate suspension.\\n\\n## Document Requests (Bonafide, Transcript, Migration Certificate)\\n- Apply at the Admin Office, Admin Block, Room A-003.\\n- Bonafide certificate: Ready in 2 working days, free of cost.\\n- Transcript: Ready in 7 working days, INR 500 per copy.\\n- Migration / Transfer Certificate: Ready in 10 working days, INR 1,000.\\n', 'source': '07_exams_and_rules.md'}\n",
      "{'text': '# SIT Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)\\n\\nQ: What is the total B.Tech fee for one year at SIT?\\nA: The B.Tech fee is INR 1,18,000 per year. In the first year, INR 10,000 admission fee and INR 5,000 refundable caution deposit are added, so the first-year total is INR 1,33,000.\\n\\nQ: Can I pay the fees in installments?\\nA: Yes. 60% must be paid before 15 July and the remaining 40% before 15 December.\\n\\nQ: Where is the CSE HOD cabin?\\nA: The CSE HOD, Dr. Anjali Sharma, sits in Block A, 3rd Floor, Room A-301.\\n\\nQ: When can I meet the CSE HOD?\\nA: Dr. Anjali Sharma is free on Monday 2:35–4:00 PM, Wednesday 11:00 AM–12:50 PM, and Friday 1:40–3:30 PM. She is not available on Tuesdays and Saturdays.\\n\\nQ: What time does college start and end?\\nA: Classes run from 9:00 AM to 4:25 PM, Monday to Friday. On Saturday, classes are from 9:00 AM to 1:00 PM. 2nd and 4th Saturdays are holidays.\\n\\nQ: What are the library timings?\\nA: The Central Library is open 8:00 AM – 8:00 PM, Monday to Saturday, and 10:00 AM – 2:00 PM on Sunday (reading room only). During exams it stays open till 10:00 PM.\\n\\nQ: How much attendance is required?\\nA: Minimum 75% in each subject.\\n\\nQ: Who do I contact for a bonafide certificate?\\nA: Apply at the Admin Office, Admin Block, Room A-003. It is ready in 2 working days and is free.\\n\\nQ: Is there a hostel facility for girls?\\nA: Yes. The Girls Hostel is in the south campus near Block D, with 400 seats. Warden: Mrs. Pooja Saxena (0731-2400302).\\n\\nQ: What is the late fee penalty?\\nA: INR 100 per day after the due date, up to a maximum of INR 5,000.\\n\\nQ: Where is the placement cell?\\nA: Training & Placement Cell is in Admin Block, 1st Floor, Room A-110. TPO: Mr. Amit Bansal.\\n', 'source': '08_faq.md'}\n"
     ]
